  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Mexogenin may interact with SNU-387 through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Mexogenin is predicted to target Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn is a target of Sasanquasaponin I and Npc126240, both of which also target SNU-387. This indicates a potential pathway where Mexogenin influences SNU-387 via multiple intermediate proteins. The scores from the three paths, ranging from 0.5211 to 0.5306, suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain. The evidence highlights the role of microtubule-associated proteins in mediating the effect of Mexogenin on SNU-387, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mechanisms involved."
